571:**E3 — Inductor graph-partition test (PyGraph positioning).** Arm C1P = C1 (public path, `mode="reduce-overhead"`, no repairs) with `torch._inductor.config.graph_partition=True` (`fullmodel/fullarms.py`), matched against C1 at 352,800 only, m1–m3; one node-level trace of C1P with graph verification (launch and staging-copy counts) and `TORCH_LOGS=cudagraphs` skip reasons (`torchlogs_*C1P*.log`). Observed before registration: C1 at 8 s runs 96 graph launches and 63 staging-copy kernels per pass (`docs/phase3/x1/x1_decomposition_352800.json`). Prediction (registered): no material change, |C1 − C1P| < 2 % of C1 wall (< 0.7 ms), ≈ 96 launches and ≈ 63 staging kernels, because the fragmentation is a Dynamo break at `_asdict` that Inductor partitioning cannot merge. If partition does help, F2 becomes a partition finding and is reported as such. Validation: loose tier; no SDR gate (numerics identical to C1). Kill: none.
573:**E2 — Repair × max-autotune.** C3 is built on `mode="reduce-overhead"` (`fullarms.py:88`, confirmed). Arm C3M = C3 repairs + `mode="max-autotune"` (cudagraphs included), matched against C3 at both operating points, m1–m3; FULLY_GRAPHED required (graph verification of the C3M node trace); kernel counts and the Triton GEMM-template selection recorded from the trace (`traces/template_count_{C3,C3M}_*.json`); SDR gate on C3M r1 at both operating points. Observed before registration: C2 (max-autotune without the repairs) was UNTESTED-by-allowance at 8 s in session 1. Prediction, *default*: at 8 s C3M faster than C3 by ≥ 1.0 ms and ≤ 4.48 ms (part of X2 realized by template epilogue fusion); at 4,410 within noise (|Δ| ≤ 0.05 ms). Kill: if C3M is INVALID (gate or validation) at an operating point, the cell is reported and E4a uses C3 as control.
575:**E1 — X6a, weight re-cast removal.** (a) Arm C3F = C3 + `torch._inductor.config.freezing=True` before compile; composition with cudagraph trees and the C3 repair is what the pair tests. Matched against C3 at both operating points, m1–m3; node traces of C3 and C3F at both; cast-kernel count and time per pass before/after (`traces/cast_count_*.json`, kernel-name match on `_to_copy`); SDR gate on C3F r1. Validation: registered loose tier (compiled arm); the cast values are identical, so a tight-tier agreement is expected and reported if observed. (b) Contingency arm C3P (`fullmodel/precast.py`): the band-split and mask-estimator Linear weights cast to fp16 once at install (external module swap), everything else public; run iff C3F is not an eligible pair at an operating point or leaves ≥ 50 % of C3's cast kernels (`e1_branch.json`, decided in-session by the registered rule). Observed before registration: X6a = 0.9198 ms at 8 s and 0.8574 ms at 4,410 (`LEDGER.md` X6a). Prediction, *default*: realized ≥ 0.7 × 0.857 ms = 0.60 ms at 4,410 and ≥ 0.6 × 0.920 ms = 0.55 ms at 8 s. Kill: if the SDR gate fails, stop the E1 lane and report.
577:**E9 — Held-out crossover prediction (the anchor experiment; runs before E4a and E5).** Cost model `docs/phase3/probes/e9_cost_model.py` → `docs/phase3/e9/e9_cost_model.json` (sha256 recorded in `session3_config.json`), built ONLY from the 8 s and 100 ms trace decompositions (`docs/phase3/padbatch/decomposition_table.json`) and the four existing sweep points (headline walls at 4,410, 22,050, 88,200, 352,800). Terms of D(L) = wall(C3, L) − wall(H, L) (+ = H faster): fixed batching benefit B = 0.567 ms; non-GEMM front/tail and transformer-middle deltas linear in frames F = L/441 + 1; padded FLOPs 0.1609 GFLOP/frame at rate_H(F); kernel-efficiency term 0.4086 GFLOP/frame × (1/rate_H − 1/rate_C3) with saturating rate curves R·F/(F+h). Twelve variants were computed; the registered variant is the one with the smallest maximum in-sample residual, chosen before any held-out measurement: `sweep_refit_THNone_TCNone` (in-sample residuals at 4,410/22,050/88,200/352,800: +0.179, +0.140, -0.418, +0.093 ms; the 88,200 point is the hardest for every variant). **Registered predictions:** crossover L* = 261,072 samples (5.92 s); D(176,400) = +0.368 ms (H faster); D(264,600) = -0.015 ms (C3 faster by less than the model's own in-sample error, so the sign test at 6 s is weak and the magnitude test is the operative one; recorded as such). The traces-only variant (no sweep refit) gives L* = 219,177, D(176,400) = +0.188, D(264,600) = -0.200 and is recorded as the secondary reading. Already observed before this registration: 4,410, 22,050, 88,200 and 352,800; only 176,400 (4 s) and 264,600 (6 s) are held out, and those two lengths are never run on the shakedown host or in any ad-hoc process (`fullarms.held_out_guard`, `SESSION_POD=1` only inside the pod session). Measurement: eager-A validation references at both lengths, then matched C3 vs H, m1–m3, with the E6 A/A block (C3 vs C3, m1) at each length, protocol 5a. Pass (registered): predicted sign correct at both lengths and |observed − predicted| ≤ 0.4 ms at both (`e_tools.py e9_check`, observed = median over eligible restarts of the block medians, block-level bootstrap interval reported). Fail: report which term the residual points at (the per-term values are stored in the registration); do not refit and re-run.
579:**E4a — X2, norm-scale folding as a wrapper (wrapper class; allowed).** Arm C3N = C3 repairs + `fullmodel/foldnorm.py` (RMSNorm gamma folded into the following `to_qkv`, `to_gates` and feed-forward first Linear once at install; GEMM on the un-normalized input; per-token scale s(x) = √dim / max(‖x‖₂, 1e-12) applied after the GEMM in the epilogue position, never in the inner loop; bias after the scale; residual adds and the Transformer output norm untouched; band split and mask estimator untouched; folded weights kept fp32 so autocast behaviour equals C3's), compiled under the mode E2 selects: control = C3M and `mode="max-autotune"` iff C3M beat C3 at 8 s by ≥ 1.0 ms (the E2 prediction floor), else control = C3 and `reduce-overhead` (`e4a_decision.json`, in-session by this rule). Matched against the control at both operating points, m1–m3; SDR gate on all eight clips (C3N r1 at both operating points; per-clip outcomes recorded; the model has one stem); node traces of C3N at both. Validation: loose tier (rounding points move). Observed before registration: X2a = 1.1275 ms ceiling at 8 s and 0.0154 ms at 4,410 (`LEDGER.md` X2a). Prediction, *default*: realized ≥ 0.5 ms over its control at 8 s (half the X2a ceiling; the fold removes the norm kernels' write+read of the normalized activation, and the epilogue fusion of the scale depends on the mode) and |Δ| ≤ 0.1 ms at 4,410. Kill: if the SDR gate fails on the public checkpoint, the row is reported as "realized on speed, blocked on quality"; the gate is not tuned.
581:**E4b — RoPE folded into the QKV GEMM epilogue.** Kernel-class; owner's lane; not run by the agent. The ledger notes that E2's template epilogue fusion may capture part of it; the C3M trace reports whether the RoPE kernels survived (`template_count` and the kernel names in `traces/trace_C3M_*_cuda_gpu_kern_sum.csv`).
583:**E5 — Structural-variation boundary test (optional; allowance 3,600 s).** Same model built through the pinned construction path (`get_model_from_config` on a derived yaml, `fullmodel/variants.py`) with depth ∈ {1, 6} × mask-estimator hidden width ∈ {full (mlp_expansion_factor 4), quarter (1)}, random weights (seed 20260921), timing only; validation = self-consistency against the variant's own eager-A reference (loose tier; no SDR claim). Arms C3 and H at both operating points, two restarts each (tags `v_<variant>_r1/r2`); node traces of C3 and H per variant at 4,410 (cast time, boundary count via graph verification, kernel sum and span via timing views); weight bytes per pass from parameter counts × 2 (`param_bytes_fp16` in every run record). The public architecture is depth 6 × full, so `d6_mfull` is the random-weight control for the headline arms. Predictions (registered): (i) C3's cast time and the boundary count are invariant to depth within 10 %; (ii) the 4,410 wall floor moves with mask-estimator weight bytes with slope ≈ bytes / 1.79 TB/s; (iii) transformer time scales linearly with depth. Kill: if the cast time scales with depth, the fixed-cost explanation is wrong; report it.
585:**E7 — PDL evidence (optional; runs last).** `fullmodel/boundary_bench.py` re-run with the launch attributes recorded (Triton 3.4 `launch_pdl=True` → `cudaLaunchAttributeProgrammaticStreamSerialization`), `griddepcontrol.wait/launch_dependents` confirmed in PTX and the SASS of the compiled cubin disassembled with Triton's bundled `cuobjdump`/`nvdisasm` (mnemonics recorded as data), plus new `prologue/*` chains (a kernel with ~4,096 dependent FMAs of register work before `griddepcontrol.wait`, N ∈ {100, 1000}) so that PDL has something to overlap; one node-level trace of all chains with per-segment overlap statistics (negative inter-kernel gaps). Observed before registration: trivial-chain slopes 4.883 / 0.732 / 0.579 µs per node (stream / graph / PDL graph) and serial gaps 0.288 / 0.160 µs. Prediction, *default*: the prologue chains show a per-node PDL saving ≥ 0.5 µs in graph mode (comparable to FlashInfer's ≈ 0.4 µs per decode cell on B200) and the trace shows overlapping kernel intervals in the PDL segments; the trivial-chain saving of 0.15 µs per node reproduces within 0.05 µs. If no overlap is observed in any PDL segment, the finding is "no PDL overlap on SM120 under these attributes" and the 0.58 µs/node figure is withdrawn from the ledger.
587:**E8 — Apollo transfer.** Not registered (owner has not reopened it).
589:**Session plan (handoff §4).** Before the pod: every arm, wrapper and script above built and run end-to-end as a complete session on the shakedown host (GPU 4, tmux, `SHAKEDOWN=1`: E9 held-out cells recorded UNTESTED by rule and never run), on-node audit COMPLETE on that engineering data, one codex gate on the specs and the measurement path closed; the owner's go-ahead was given on 2026-09-21 for the measurement pod only ("only as instructed in the instructions"), and is requested again with the shakedown verdict attached before the pod is created. Order on the pod: E6 → E3 → E2 → E1 → E9 → E4a → E5 → E7. Stop and report, without retrying, if any planted fault passes, the SDR gate fails for a headline arm, clocks drift > 5 % between compared blocks, graph verification fails for an arm claimed graphed, a registered kill branch fires, or pod time exceeds 6 hours. Budget: `SESSION_BUDGET_S` 19,800 s (5.5 h) with a 900 s extraction reserve; target ≤ 3 GPU-h with E5/E7 as the registered cuts.
